Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Machine learning models often look excellent on benchmark datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.88,0:00:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then break the moment they hit real production data.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.28,0:00:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper by Matthew Groh at the MIT Media Lab argues that the usual explanation,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.65,0:00:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}distribution shift, is the wrong frame.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.20,0:00:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Distribution shift only measures that two datasets differ; it never tells you why.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.56,0:00:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Groh introduces context shift,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.52,0:00:28.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the semantically meaningful changes in how data are created, collected,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.16,0:00:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and curated that actually drive those failures,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.24,0:00:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and lays out three concrete ways to address it: leaning on human intuition and expert knowledge,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.52,0:00:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}building dynamic benchmarks, and clearly stating a model's limitations.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.46,0:00:47.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Benchmark datasets play two roles: they let researchers compare methods,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.09,0:00:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and they stand in as an imperfect model of the real world.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.82,0:00:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The trouble is that a single static benchmark can never fully capture the dynamic,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.09,0:00:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}high-dimensional complexity of real tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.80,0:01:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}So models that appear to match or beat human-level accuracy on a benchmark routinely err
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.45,0:01:08.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on out-of-distribution and adversarially perturbed production data.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.76,0:01:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The field describes this gap as distribution shift,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.04,0:01:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with subcategories like covariate shift, prior probability shift, and concept shift.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.45,0:01:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But these definitions are over-specified for comparing two data samples and under-specified
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.30,0:01:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}for evaluating the data-generating process that actually drives the mismatch.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.55,0:01:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior work treats robustness as a difference between two distributions while disregarding
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.24,0:01:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the reasons behind that difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.94,0:01:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But the difference is merely a symptom; the disease is in how data are created,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.63,0:01:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}collected, and curated.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.33,0:01:46.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As Figure 1 shows,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.02,0:01:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}interest in distribution shift terminology has grown enormously over the last decade,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.71,0:01:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with covariate shift papers alone climbing toward nine thousand per year by 2021.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.41,0:01:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Despite this volume,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.10,0:02:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the vocabulary stays tangled and rarely points practitioners toward the upstream,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.80,0:02:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}semantically meaningful factors they can actually intervene on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.79,0:02:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This is a perspective paper that reframes the robustness problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.94,0:02:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Its central contribution is the concept of context shift,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.58,0:02:18.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which describes the semantically meaningful upstream factors, sample selection bias,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.94,0:02:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}adversarial perturbation, and non-stationarity,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.94,0:02:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that drive the distribution shifts we observe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.88,0:02:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On top of that framing,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.35,0:02:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Groh identifies three practical methods for closing the benchmark-to-production gap,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.71,0:02:38.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and illustrates all of them through three recurring case-study domains: facial expression recognition,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.22,0:02:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}deepfake detection, and medical diagnosis.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.20,0:02:45.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Context refers to the semantically meaningful upstream factors that drive a distribution shift.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.28,0:02:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rather than fixating on the difference between two distributions,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.35,0:02:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Groh asks researchers to reason about the three processes that generate that difference: sample selection bias,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.43,0:02:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}for example a new dataset drawn from a demographic absent from the old one;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.51,0:03:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}adversarial perturbations, imperceptible noise injections that change model behavior;
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.59,0:03:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and non-stationarity, where the world itself moves on,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.66,0:03:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}like smartphones after 2018 versus flip phones before 2010.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.74,0:03:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three methods follow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.82,0:03:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.89,0:03:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}human intuition and expert knowledge can identify the semantically meaningful features
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.97,0:03:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on which models are likely to fail.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.05,0:03:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.12,0:03:34.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}dynamic benchmarking replaces a single static test set with continual evaluation against a well-specified,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.20,0:03:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}quality-controlled data-generation process, producing corroborated accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.28,0:03:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the distribution of scores across many benchmarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.36,0:03:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, authors should clarify a model's limitations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.43,0:03:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}explicitly stating the contexts in which performance is known and unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.81,0:03:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rather than introducing a new dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.44,0:03:57.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the paper dissects existing benchmarks across three domains.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.60,0:04:01.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In facial expression recognition it examines seven benchmarks,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.90,0:04:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from SFEW and MMI to CK+ and MultiPie.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.53,0:04:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In deepfake detection it centers on the DFDC dataset, the largest to date,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.66,0:04:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with over one hundred twenty-eight thousand videos from nine hundred sixty consenting actors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.10,0:04:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In medical diagnosis it looks at store-and-forward teledermatology and the Diverse Dermatology Images dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.72,0:04:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Throughout, it holds up context-aware benchmarks like BREEDS, WILDS,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.43,0:04:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and Dynabench as models for capturing the data-generation process instead of a single static snapshot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.80,0:04:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline evidence is how wildly performance swings with the benchmark.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.16,0:04:44.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}One facial expression model, built on AlexNet,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.52,0:04:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}ranges from just 48.6 percent accuracy on SFEW to 94.8 percent on MultiPie,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.89,0:04:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}against a random baseline of 14.2 percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.25,0:04:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so which benchmark you pick determines the story you tell.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.61,0:05:01.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The pattern generalizes: when researchers faithfully recreated the ImageNet and CIFAR-10 test sets,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.97,0:05:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}state-of-the-art accuracy fell by three to fifteen percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.33,0:05:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And a leading DFDC deepfake detector assigned only two and eight percent likelihood to
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.69,0:05:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}genuine deepfakes of Kim Jong-un and Vladimir Putin,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.06,0:05:19.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}precisely the high-context videos that matter in the real world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.42,0:05:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In dermatology,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.78,0:05:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}benchmarks that barely include dark skin let systematic errors hide in plain sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.44,0:05:31.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers anchor the argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.12,0:05:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A single facial expression model spans 48.6 to 94.8 percent accuracy across seven benchmarks,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.47,0:05:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}next to a 14.2 percent random baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.55,0:05:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Faithfully recreated ImageNet and CIFAR-10 test sets cut state-of-the-art accuracy by three to fifteen percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.31,0:05:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A leading deepfake detector gave only two and eight percent likelihood to real deepfakes of world leaders.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.68,0:06:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The DFDC benchmark holds 128,154 videos from 960 actors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.11,0:06:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And one dermatology benchmark included just 2.7 percent of the second-darkest skin type,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.06,0:06:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a single person of the darkest.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.12,0:06:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message is a shift in perspective: stop treating the benchmark-to-production
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.45,0:06:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gap as a mere statistical distance between two datasets and start treating it as context
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.79,0:06:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}shift,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.12,0:06:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the semantically meaningful changes in how data are generated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.45,0:06:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Address it by pairing machine learning with human intuition and expertise,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.79,0:06:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}by moving from static to dynamic benchmarks that evaluate the data-generation process,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.12,0:06:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and by clearly clarifying each model's limitations.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.45,0:06:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The simplest and most immediately effective step is honesty: state plainly the contexts
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.79,0:06:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}in which a model has been evaluated and the contexts in which its behavior remains unknown.
